<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ovamboland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Owamboland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ovamboland is the region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> inhabited by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovambo-people">Ovambo people</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etosha-pan">Etosha Pan</a> and the Angolan border. German rule hardly reached it, but after 1915 it came under South African administration and was later made an apartheid-era <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> with its own legislative council. It supplied much of the colony's migrant labour and became the heartland of support for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swapo">SWAPO</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ovamboland.jpg" alt="Ovamboland" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mysid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ovamboland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
